/**
 * @mainpage Programming Project II - Register Allocation Tool
 *
 * @section intro Introduction
 * Tool for performing graph-coloring register allocation on variable live ranges.
 * Live ranges are parsed from an input file, merged into webs, and an interference
 * graph is built. Four allocation algorithms are available, ranging from a simple
 * Chaitin simplification to DSatur with articulation-point heuristics.
 *
 * @section algorithms Allocation Algorithms
 * - **basic** — Chaitin simplification with optimistic coloring; if any web cannot
 *   be colored all webs are assigned to memory.
 * - **spilling** — iteratively forces the highest-degree web to memory and retries
 *   basic allocation, up to a configurable maximum number of spills.
 * - **splitting** — iteratively splits the web whose partition best reduces
 *   interference pressure and retries basic allocation, up to a configurable
 *   maximum number of splits.
 * - **free** — DSatur greedy coloring with tie-breaking by degree and articulation
 *   points; minimises spills without a forced-spill budget.
 *
 * @section structure Project Structure
 * - **parser** — reads and parses the ranges and registers input files
 * - **webs** — merges overlapping live ranges of each variable into webs
 * - **graph_builder** — builds the undirected interference graph from webs
 * - **register_allocation** — basic, spilling, splitting, and DSatur allocators
 * - **output** — writes the allocation results to the output file
 * - **pipeline** — orchestrates the full workflow
 * - **menu** — interactive command-line interface
 *
 * @section authors Authors
 * - Nuno Gonçalves
 * - Raquel Silva
 */